What you need to know:

Financial:

· Meet individual underwriting expectations to help team achieve budgeted financial objectives.



Business Process:

· Underwrite within agreed decision making standards, limitations, and underwriting authority;

· Assess desirability of risk through analysis of broker submission, NAT CAT modelling and survey reports (as required)); regular contact with broker; thorough review of proposal; and review of claims history and general company information;

· Use designated Underwriting system(s) to streamline underwriting and information- tracking approach across Profit Centre. Input required data consistently and accurately;

· Provide accurate monthly Management information including, but not limited to, submissions, bind rate, average premium, and total premium as required



Customer and Sales:

· Provide excellent service to brokers through consistent, timely, and proactive approach to underwriting;

· Exhibit sales orientated behaviours, defined by Management as: motivated, tenacious, focused, technically skilled, proactive, and accountable;

· Generate new business by expanding broker network, attending broker events, and building new relationships across the market;

· Provide training to brokers on property products as required either on one – to – one basis or as group presentation;

· Provide support to broker by attending client meetings or providing client presentations as required;

· Work with Property leader to execute sales plan in identification of brokers and products to target

· Take responsibility for meeting individual new business targets set by Property Leader

· Take responsibility for individual allocation of renewals.



People:

· Liaise with Commercial Operations Team as policy and/or booking issues arise;

· Work with the underwriters within the team to help build their knowledge in order to grow and develop;

· Build relationships with brokers by attending and organising regular broker events;

· Ensure all brokers and clients are treated fairly;

· Ensure customer-centric approach.



Reporting/Compliance/Technical:

· Progress towards achieving minimum competency level as required and within the necessary timeframe;

· Gain an understanding of relevant policy coverage, any minimum terms and conditions applicable, insurance program structures, risk management etc.;

· Conduct peer reviews as required;

· Ensure compliance with key regulatory and risk management responsibilities.



 What we’re looking for:

· Property Underwriting experience or Property lines insurance broking is essential; other relevant professional experience may substitute for underwriting experience;

· Strong communication skills;

· Strong interpersonal skills and team-spirited approach;

· Time management - ability to handle multiple priorities, organise work and meet deadlines;

· Strong analytical and technical skills;

· Ability to network and build relationships;

· Attention to Detail

· Organizational skill

· Customer and sales focused;

· Tenacious, motivated, proactive.

